 {
-    /* Shared monotonic PLL index the v4 firmware reads directly: idx = MHz/10 - 18,
+    /* Shared monotonic PLL index the v5+ firmware reads directly: idx = MHz/10 - 18,
        clamped to the mode-0x10 ladder [8,32] (~260-500 MHz). clk==0 keeps the
        firmware default/off path. The old ((clk/10)%20)+2 form was non-monotonic and
        could not emit indices 22-32, so distinct MHz collapsed onto the same low PLL
        entries (e.g. 400->code2 and 520->code14 both read ~150 GH/s). On stock
